269
00:22:04,027 --> 00:22:06,062
-What?
-I'm begging you.

270
00:22:23,747 --> 00:22:26,183
FROM YU

271
00:22:34,458 --> 00:22:36,960
DIVORCE FORM

272
00:22:42,499 --> 00:22:43,900
YU UKITA

273
00:23:28,311 --> 00:23:31,248
You're showing signs of depression.

274
00:23:33,250 --> 00:23:35,085
Please do not overexert yourself at work,

275
00:23:35,619 --> 00:23:37,721
and try to eliminate
environmental stressors

276
00:23:37,787 --> 00:23:38,922
as much as possible.

277
00:23:41,391 --> 00:23:43,727
Do you have any family members
that can provide support?

278
00:23:49,032 --> 00:23:49,866
No.

279
00:23:57,407 --> 00:23:59,876
I haven't drawn in so long,
I'm a little nervous.

280
00:23:59,943 --> 00:24:01,378
Yeah, it's a bit nerve-wracking.

281
00:24:01,444 --> 00:24:03,079
Thank you for coming today.

282
00:24:03,146 --> 00:24:05,348
It's so nostalgic.

283
00:24:05,415 --> 00:24:06,716
This was drawn using crayons.

284
00:24:07,951 --> 00:24:08,852
Welcome.

285
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:10,754
Please come inside.

286
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:12,355
No, I'm all right.

287
00:24:13,957 --> 00:24:15,158
Please come in.

288
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:20,630
You may not be very familiar
with the concept of art therapy,

289
00:24:20,697 --> 00:24:22,332
but it is a therapeutic approach

290
00:24:22,399 --> 00:24:26,036
in which you engage with your inner self
and sort through your feelings

291
00:24:26,102 --> 00:24:28,371
with activities such as drawing
or working with clay.

292
00:24:29,573 --> 00:24:31,007
And please be rest assured,

293
00:24:31,074 --> 00:24:33,810
despite the name,
you do not need any artistic skills.

294
00:24:34,678 --> 00:24:35,912
Are you relieved?

295
00:24:37,047 --> 00:24:40,917
Today, please draw a landscape
that is memorable to you,

296
00:24:40,984 --> 00:24:42,118
or perhaps the sky.

297
00:24:42,953 --> 00:24:44,187
Please begin.

298
00:24:44,254 --> 00:24:46,256
Please relax and enjoy drawing.

299
00:24:46,323 --> 00:24:48,458
-What should I draw?
-Enjoy.

300
00:25:01,471 --> 00:25:03,573
You painted a view of the sky by the sea.

301
00:25:04,741 --> 00:25:05,709
Yes.

302
00:25:07,510 --> 00:25:09,012
What kind of memories do you have here?

303
00:25:10,714 --> 00:25:13,216
There's no specific "memory," but…

304
00:25:29,299 --> 00:25:31,034
Are these footprints?

305
00:25:33,803 --> 00:25:34,704
Yes.

306
00:25:37,641 --> 00:25:39,476
You must've walked quite a distance.

307
00:25:47,384 --> 00:25:49,319
I really felt like I was doing my best,

308
00:25:51,521 --> 00:25:53,456
but it seems
I was just spinning my wheels…

309
00:25:55,692 --> 00:25:58,361
Even the things I did
with my son's best interests at heart

310
00:25:59,629 --> 00:26:00,797
turned out to be wrong.

311
00:26:06,202 --> 00:26:07,203
I'm sorry.

312
00:26:07,971 --> 00:26:09,939
No need to apologize.

313
00:26:11,207 --> 00:26:12,742
You can talk about anything here.

314
00:26:20,383 --> 00:26:21,518
What's the matter?

315
00:26:29,059 --> 00:26:30,460
Both family and work

316
00:26:31,561 --> 00:26:33,296
can be lost in an instant.

317
00:26:39,369 --> 00:26:40,270
This…

318
00:26:43,173 --> 00:26:45,675
is scenery I'll never get to see
ever again.

319
00:27:05,528 --> 00:27:06,396
I'm sorry.

320
00:27:06,463 --> 00:27:08,665
-No worries.
-Thanks.

321
00:27:11,334 --> 00:27:14,170
Do you draw often, Mr. Tatsuki?

322
00:27:14,237 --> 00:27:17,040
Yes. I studied design at university.

323
00:27:17,107 --> 00:27:20,210
No wonder you're so good.

324
00:27:20,744 --> 00:27:22,112
Do you draw too?

325
00:27:22,178 --> 00:27:24,314
No, I specialize in psychology

326
00:27:24,380 --> 00:27:26,082
and I'm terrible at drawing.

327
00:27:27,183 --> 00:27:29,853
But art is very useful
when trying to confront oneself.

328
00:27:32,055 --> 00:27:33,189
I see.

329
00:27:36,593 --> 00:27:38,962
-Mr. Tatsuki.
-Yes?

330
00:27:39,529 --> 00:27:40,997
Do you have time after this?

331
00:27:42,098 --> 00:27:42,932
What?

332
00:27:42,999 --> 00:27:44,567
YUKANAI

333
00:27:44,634 --> 00:27:45,635
NOW ACCEPTING NEW STUDENTS

334
00:27:45,702 --> 00:27:47,203
This way. Please come in.

335
00:27:47,270 --> 00:27:48,371
Thank you.

336
00:27:48,438 --> 00:27:49,572
Hey everyone.

337
00:27:50,140 --> 00:27:52,275
-Hello.
-Hello.

338
00:27:53,710 --> 00:27:56,846
This is the alternative school
that I founded.

339
00:27:56,913 --> 00:27:58,314
-Alternative school?
-Yes.

340
00:27:58,982 --> 00:28:02,585
I wanted to create a safe space
for children who,

341
00:28:03,286 --> 00:28:04,387
for various reasons,

342
00:28:04,954 --> 00:28:06,289
find it hard to attend school.

343
00:28:07,357 --> 00:28:08,525
I see.

344
00:28:09,692 --> 00:28:10,827
Oh, you're drawing.

345
00:28:10,894 --> 00:28:12,762
Look at this.

346
00:28:12,829 --> 00:28:14,197
You're so good.

347
00:28:14,264 --> 00:28:15,832
-Really?
-Yeah.

348
00:28:15,899 --> 00:28:17,934
-Look.
-How cute.

349
00:28:18,001 --> 00:28:20,336
-Look at this.
-Isn't this funny?

350
00:28:20,403 --> 00:28:21,704
That's cute.

351
00:28:22,872 --> 00:28:24,207
This way.

352
00:28:24,841 --> 00:28:25,675
Okay.

353
00:28:26,709 --> 00:28:28,812
I'm thinking it'd be nice
to offer art therapy here

354
00:28:28,878 --> 00:28:30,814
as a way to tie it in
with my own research.

355
00:28:31,714 --> 00:28:32,782
I see.

356
00:28:33,583 --> 00:28:34,951
Would you like to work here with me?

357
00:28:35,952 --> 00:28:36,953
What?

358
00:28:37,020 --> 00:28:38,421
You quit your other job, right?

359
00:28:38,488 --> 00:28:40,390
Yeah, but…

360
00:28:41,157 --> 00:28:44,394
You lost everything
triggered by the issue of school refusal,

361
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:47,230
and now you're at rock bottom, aren't you?

362
00:28:47,297 --> 00:28:48,765
You're so brutally honest.

363
00:28:49,799 --> 00:28:50,934
Are you good with games?

364
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,502
Not really.

365
00:28:52,569 --> 00:28:54,871
But you can draw.

366
00:28:54,938 --> 00:28:56,773
-I think you're suitable for this job.
-Um…

367
00:28:58,408 --> 00:29:00,343
I'm very thankful for the offer,

368
00:29:01,077 --> 00:29:02,812
but why me, we've only just met?

369
00:29:05,949 --> 00:29:06,950
My intuition, I guess.

370
00:29:09,219 --> 00:29:10,053
What?

371
00:29:11,020 --> 00:29:13,056
-I'm first.
-No, it's me.

372
00:29:13,122 --> 00:29:14,824
-It's my turn.
-No, it's me.

373
00:29:14,891 --> 00:29:15,925
-Hey, hey.
-Let go.

374
00:29:15,992 --> 00:29:18,161
You have to take turns.

375
00:29:18,228 --> 00:29:19,863
-Or someone will get hurt.
-It's my turn.

376
00:29:19,929 --> 00:29:21,731
Wow, that was consecutive.

377
00:29:22,398 --> 00:29:23,766
Seiryu,

378
00:29:23,833 --> 00:29:26,069
clean up after yourself.
Don't leave things out.

379
00:29:26,135 --> 00:29:27,337
I didn't do that.

380
00:29:27,403 --> 00:29:28,304
Huh?

381
00:29:36,646 --> 00:29:39,549
Who wants to play in the courtyard?

382
00:29:42,218 --> 00:29:44,087
-So, about this…
-Yeah?

383
00:29:44,153 --> 00:29:45,355
Haruhi, Kurumi, wanna play?

384
00:29:46,155 --> 00:29:48,124
-No, I'm okay.
-No thanks.

385
00:29:48,191 --> 00:29:51,694
-Soya, let's play <i>Mario Party</i>.
-You're not going to play soccer?

386
00:29:51,761 --> 00:29:53,162
No, Mr. Tatsuki is scary.

387
00:29:53,229 --> 00:29:54,764
-Oh…
-Let's play games.

388
00:29:54,831 --> 00:29:56,966
-Okay…
-I wanna play with you too.

389
00:29:57,033 --> 00:29:59,035
Oh no, hold on.

390
00:29:59,869 --> 00:30:01,738
That was close.

391
00:30:01,804 --> 00:30:02,739
Watch out!

392
00:30:14,584 --> 00:30:16,586
Mr. Tatsuki, are you all right?

393
00:30:24,560 --> 00:30:26,596
Oh my god.

394
00:30:26,663 --> 00:30:28,598
It's Café-Au-Lait Man!

395
00:30:29,666 --> 00:30:31,034
No, he's a zombie.

396
00:30:31,100 --> 00:30:33,603
You're right. He's a zombie.

397
00:30:35,238 --> 00:30:38,207
-Café-Au-Lait Zombie.
-Hey, zombie.

398
00:30:38,274 --> 00:30:41,044
A zombie! A zombie!

399
00:30:41,110 --> 00:30:44,681
A zombie! A zombie!

400
00:30:44,747 --> 00:30:46,316
Who are you calling a zombie?

401
00:30:53,623 --> 00:30:55,425
The zombie is here.

402
00:31:08,838 --> 00:31:11,074
Peter Piper picked a peck
of pickled peppers…

403
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:13,276
Good morning.

404
00:31:14,077 --> 00:31:14,911
What the…?

405
00:31:15,511 --> 00:31:17,747
What?

406
00:31:17,814 --> 00:31:18,681
What do you think?

407
00:31:18,748 --> 00:31:20,016
Your hair color changed.

408
00:31:20,616 --> 00:31:21,851
A makeover? That's nice.

409
00:31:21,918 --> 00:31:23,686
You look like Super Saiyan.

410
00:31:23,753 --> 00:31:25,822
-You're Super Saiyan!
-It's gross.

411
00:31:25,888 --> 00:31:27,090
Who said it was gross?

412
00:31:27,156 --> 00:31:29,726
The look suits you.

413
00:31:29,792 --> 00:31:31,761
You look like a nice fairy.

414
00:31:32,628 --> 00:31:33,796
Thank you.

415
00:31:33,863 --> 00:31:35,665
-Mr. Tatsuki.
-Yeah?

416
00:31:35,732 --> 00:31:37,000
I want to draw.

417
00:31:37,700 --> 00:31:38,568
Okay.

418
00:31:38,634 --> 00:31:42,338
But from now on,
you can just call me Tatsuki.

419
00:31:42,405 --> 00:31:45,441
-Tatsuki, can we use the atelier?
-Of course.

420
00:31:45,508 --> 00:31:47,877
-Let's go, everyone!
-Yeah.

421
00:31:47,944 --> 00:31:49,679
Wait for me.

422
00:31:49,746 --> 00:31:51,280
-Tatsuki.
-Yeah?

423
00:31:52,482 --> 00:31:53,316
Not bad.

424
00:31:54,684 --> 00:31:55,518
Shut up.

425
00:31:55,585 --> 00:31:57,787
-Not bad.
-Not bad.

426
00:31:57,854 --> 00:31:59,322
Not bad.

427
00:31:59,389 --> 00:32:01,791
-Not bad.
-Enough already.

428
00:32:01,858 --> 00:32:04,293
YUKANAI

429
00:32:18,908 --> 00:32:22,879
YU

430
00:32:25,748 --> 00:32:27,417
-Hello?
<i>-Tatsuki…</i>

431
00:32:27,483 --> 00:32:29,018
Sora… Sora…

432
00:32:30,453 --> 00:32:31,320
What about Sora?

433
00:32:31,387 --> 00:32:33,122
Sora jumped.

434
00:32:34,424 --> 00:32:35,258
What?

435
00:33:11,861 --> 00:33:12,762
Hey there.

436
00:33:14,063 --> 00:33:15,465
Hello.

437
00:33:16,699 --> 00:33:19,068
I heard that Nene's situation
isn't looking good?

438
00:33:19,802 --> 00:33:20,636
Yeah.

439
00:33:25,341 --> 00:33:27,043
<i>Is it okay if her grades keep dropping?</i>

440
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:28,778
You need to go to cram school and study.

441
00:33:28,845 --> 00:33:30,613
She loves playing the piano.

442
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:32,148
I hate playing the piano.

443
00:33:32,215 --> 00:33:34,584
-Then why didn't you say so?
-There's no way I could.

444
00:33:34,650 --> 00:33:36,018
If I do,

445
00:33:36,085 --> 00:33:38,387
you and Dad will start fighting again.

446
00:33:40,223 --> 00:33:43,159
<i>I don't want things</i>
<i>to turn out like it did with Sora.</i>

447
00:33:44,894 --> 00:33:45,928
But I don't know what to do.

448
00:33:45,995 --> 00:33:47,830
How were her parents doing?

449
00:33:50,133 --> 00:33:51,601
They're very similar

450
00:33:52,201 --> 00:33:53,603
to how I was back then.

451
00:33:55,238 --> 00:33:57,039
As if their expectations and hopes

452
00:33:57,106 --> 00:33:58,808
for their child have gone awry,

453
00:33:58,875 --> 00:34:01,077
trapping them in a vicious cycle.

454
00:34:02,845 --> 00:34:03,746
I see.

455
00:34:04,747 --> 00:34:06,883
I went to the door of her room,

456
00:34:10,286 --> 00:34:12,488
<i>but I couldn't do anything,</i>
<i>and I just left.</i>

457
00:34:18,494 --> 00:34:20,663
Why don't we invite her parents here?

458
00:34:21,964 --> 00:34:23,232
Invite them here?

459
00:34:24,333 --> 00:34:25,935
There's some art therapy
I want to try out.

460
00:34:26,569 --> 00:34:28,237
Of course, you’ll be doing it too.

461
00:34:34,544 --> 00:34:35,411
This way, please.

462
00:34:37,813 --> 00:34:38,648
Hello.

463
00:34:39,215 --> 00:34:41,484
I'm Mikumo, the representative at Yukanai.

464
00:34:43,419 --> 00:34:45,821
-Thank you for your help.
-Thank you for coming.

465
00:34:47,957 --> 00:34:49,725
Why were we called here today?

466
00:34:50,726 --> 00:34:53,296
We're all concerned about Nene,

467
00:34:53,362 --> 00:34:54,730
but we can only imagine

468
00:34:54,797 --> 00:34:57,233
that it's been a tremendous burden
on you two as well.

469
00:34:57,967 --> 00:35:02,004
So we wanted to have you
spend some time relaxing today.

470
00:35:03,206 --> 00:35:05,608
So we prepared this.

471
00:35:06,809 --> 00:35:07,643
Please sit down.

472
00:35:07,710 --> 00:35:08,844
Yes, please.

473
00:35:09,545 --> 00:35:10,513
Thank you.

474
00:35:13,516 --> 00:35:16,819
Does this have anything to do with Nene?

475
00:35:17,553 --> 00:35:18,387
Yes.

476
00:35:19,989 --> 00:35:21,857
Please bear with us
for just a little while.

477
00:35:23,826 --> 00:35:27,763
This is a traditional dyeing
and transfer technique

478
00:35:27,830 --> 00:35:29,999
called <i>suminagashi</i>.

479
00:35:30,066 --> 00:35:32,301
I'll start by showing you how it's done.

480
00:35:33,569 --> 00:35:35,037
Start by dropping

481
00:35:36,072 --> 00:35:38,107
sumi ink onto the surface of the water.

482
00:35:41,077 --> 00:35:43,145
And this is oil.

483
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:47,350
Mix the oil with the sumi ink.

484
00:35:49,185 --> 00:35:51,287
You can swirl the sumi ink like this.

485
00:35:52,154 --> 00:35:53,489
Once you're done with that,

486
00:35:53,556 --> 00:35:56,659
you can gently shake
the surface of the water,

487
00:35:57,627 --> 00:35:59,762
or you can blow on it as well.

488
00:36:03,899 --> 00:36:04,800
Oh no,

489
00:36:04,867 --> 00:36:07,103
it's not turning out the way I imagined.

490
00:36:07,169 --> 00:36:08,404
Last but not least,

491
00:36:09,038 --> 00:36:11,440
I'm going to place the paper in the water.

492
00:36:15,211 --> 00:36:17,513
This is how it turned out.

493
00:36:17,580 --> 00:36:18,948
Wow.

494
00:36:19,815 --> 00:36:21,450
Shall we all try it as well?

495
00:36:23,819 --> 00:36:24,720
Sure.

496
00:36:25,354 --> 00:36:26,789
I'll give it a try.

497
00:36:29,759 --> 00:36:32,061
Mrs. Tachibana, you're so good at this.
It's so pretty.

498
00:36:33,562 --> 00:36:34,997
You're doing well too.

499
00:36:35,598 --> 00:36:38,301
Oh no, don't go that way…

500
00:36:41,537 --> 00:36:44,073
At first, I was trying to create a dragon,

501
00:36:44,140 --> 00:36:46,008
but this is how it turned out.

502
00:36:48,711 --> 00:36:52,081
I actually put in a bit too much sumi ink
right at the start,

503
00:36:52,148 --> 00:36:56,519
so I decided to just utilize that
and simply go with the flow.

504
00:36:57,086 --> 00:36:58,454
How did you like it?

505
00:36:59,689 --> 00:37:00,756
Well,

506
00:37:01,324 --> 00:37:03,559
I couldn't control it well enough,

507
00:37:03,626 --> 00:37:04,960
so it was a bit frustrating.

508
00:37:05,528 --> 00:37:06,362
And you, Mrs. Tamami?

509
00:37:07,330 --> 00:37:11,867
It turned out completely differently
than I had imagined,

510
00:37:11,934 --> 00:37:14,570
but that actually
made it all the more fun.

511
00:37:15,137 --> 00:37:18,474
Mr. Yukio approached it with
a clear vision right from the start,

512
00:37:18,541 --> 00:37:20,810
while Mrs. Tamami simply let
the ink take its course.

513
00:37:21,377 --> 00:37:23,245
That contrast is quite fascinating.

514
00:37:24,280 --> 00:37:25,514
How about you, Tatsuki?

515
00:37:27,183 --> 00:37:28,517
With <i>suminagashi</i>,

516
00:37:28,584 --> 00:37:31,587
once you drop the ink, there's no telling
how it's going to spread, huh?

517
00:37:31,654 --> 00:37:34,790
Watching over those
unpredictable movements

518
00:37:34,857 --> 00:37:35,758
is what makes this fun.

519
00:37:37,326 --> 00:37:38,527
But

520
00:37:39,729 --> 00:37:43,466
I guess I was trying to control things
to make it turn out the way I want.

521
00:37:57,113 --> 00:38:01,517
You haven't seen
Nene's diamond art yet, have you?

522
00:38:02,084 --> 00:38:02,918
No.

523
00:38:05,421 --> 00:38:07,790
You mentioned
that she chose brown and pink

524
00:38:07,857 --> 00:38:11,761
because she thought they were colors
that'd make us happy, right?

525
00:38:11,827 --> 00:38:12,695
Yes.

526
00:38:13,763 --> 00:38:16,499
At first, she didn't have the confidence
to choose the colors herself.

527
00:38:17,400 --> 00:38:18,834
What about this foal?

528
00:38:19,702 --> 00:38:23,606
At first it was made with a mix
of brown and pink,

529
00:38:23,672 --> 00:38:25,474
because brown would make her dad happy,

530
00:38:25,541 --> 00:38:27,243
and pink is her mom's favorite color.

531
00:38:28,944 --> 00:38:30,446
But before she could show it to you guys,

532
00:38:31,046 --> 00:38:32,848
she tried to destroy it.

533
00:38:34,283 --> 00:38:37,586
<i>But she brought it with her</i>
<i>to the Yukanai Camp.</i>

534
00:38:38,154 --> 00:38:39,855
I worked so hard to make it,

535
00:38:40,790 --> 00:38:42,091
but I ended up destroying it.

536
00:38:44,894 --> 00:38:48,597
And when she decided to work on it again,

537
00:38:48,664 --> 00:38:52,101
she was finally able to tell me

538
00:38:52,768 --> 00:38:54,270
her favorite color.

539
00:39:00,009 --> 00:39:01,844
The truth is, my favorite color is blue.

540
00:39:03,712 --> 00:39:05,448
<i>As I listened closely,</i>

541
00:39:06,015 --> 00:39:09,485
I gradually began hearing the words

542
00:39:10,619 --> 00:39:13,422
she couldn't bring herself to say
until then.

543
00:39:16,358 --> 00:39:17,827
I see.

544
00:39:20,996 --> 00:39:22,431
Perhaps

545
00:39:23,799 --> 00:39:25,901
we were doing nothing but forcing

546
00:39:25,968 --> 00:39:28,137
our own feelings and expectations
onto her.

547
00:39:29,939 --> 00:39:31,006
Yeah.

548
00:39:35,244 --> 00:39:36,612
We'll try once more

549
00:39:37,446 --> 00:39:38,848
to see Nene eye to eye.

550
00:39:40,416 --> 00:39:41,684
That's wonderful.

551
00:39:42,685 --> 00:39:43,986
I think that's a great idea.

552
00:39:47,256 --> 00:39:50,392
I actually have a suggestion
for the both of you.

553
00:40:04,006 --> 00:40:08,177
NENE

554
00:40:22,391 --> 00:40:25,294
<i>We tried our hand at diamond art too.</i>

555
00:40:26,161 --> 00:40:28,664
<i>The messy part was done by Dad.</i>

556
00:40:29,298 --> 00:40:31,500
<i>Nene, please finish the rest.</i>

557
00:41:13,342 --> 00:41:15,277
NOW ACCEPTING NEW STUDENTS

558
00:41:20,649 --> 00:41:21,617
Good morning Tatsuki.

559
00:41:22,184 --> 00:41:23,752
Good morning.

560
00:41:25,220 --> 00:41:26,422
I decided not to leave.

561
00:41:26,989 --> 00:41:27,823
Huh?

562
00:41:29,124 --> 00:41:31,493
All right!

563
00:41:32,695 --> 00:41:34,630
What should I do today?

564
00:41:42,071 --> 00:41:43,505
What's this?

565
00:41:44,907 --> 00:41:47,242
That's called <i>suminagashi</i>.

566
00:41:47,309 --> 00:41:48,177
-I see.
-Oh.

567
00:41:48,243 --> 00:41:50,045
Do you want to try paper marbling?

568
00:41:50,112 --> 00:41:51,146
What is that?

569
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:53,949
It's similar to <i>suminagashi</i>
but it uses color ink.

570
00:41:54,016 --> 00:41:55,184
I want to try it.

571
00:42:09,365 --> 00:42:12,701
Your style is so free and relaxed.
It's nice.

572
00:42:12,768 --> 00:42:14,103
-Really?
-Yeah.

573
00:42:17,506 --> 00:42:20,509
How's your dad and mom lately?

574
00:42:21,543 --> 00:42:23,579
We haven't talked about anything yet.

575
00:42:24,079 --> 00:42:25,948
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

576
00:42:26,982 --> 00:42:27,816
I see.

577
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:34,957
But I think it's going to be okay now.

578
00:42:38,460 --> 00:42:39,294
Okay.

579
00:42:42,331 --> 00:42:43,332
Tatsuki…

580
00:42:45,734 --> 00:42:46,669
Thank you.

581
00:42:49,438 --> 00:42:51,340
-Say that again?
-Never mind.

582
00:42:55,310 --> 00:42:56,979
Tatsuki, do you have a kid?

583
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,748
Yeah.

584
00:43:00,849 --> 00:43:02,685
You have to take good care of your family.

585
00:43:04,787 --> 00:43:07,589
-Why do you say that?
-I just felt like I had to say it.

586
00:43:09,425 --> 00:43:10,259
‎I see.

587
00:43:22,137 --> 00:43:24,206
All right, I'm done.

588
00:43:27,676 --> 00:43:28,711
Pull the paper up.

589
00:43:30,879 --> 00:43:32,514
-Ta-da.
-Wow.

590
00:43:32,581 --> 00:43:33,782
How is it?

591
00:43:34,450 --> 00:43:36,719
-Does it look nice?
-Very nice.

592
00:43:36,785 --> 00:43:37,653
Thanks.

593
00:43:38,420 --> 00:43:39,254
All right.

594
00:43:39,321 --> 00:43:41,390
-It's beautiful.
-So pretty.

595
00:43:41,957 --> 00:43:44,026
-The orange color adds a nice accent.
-Yeah.

596
00:44:17,059 --> 00:44:18,160
I'll be going now.

597
00:44:18,227 --> 00:44:20,129
Bye.

598
00:44:20,195 --> 00:44:21,063
Keep at it.

599
00:44:21,563 --> 00:44:22,598
Thanks.

600
00:44:23,332 --> 00:44:24,233
NOW ACCEPTING NEW STUDENTS

601
00:45:02,070 --> 00:45:03,038
Garbage…

602
00:45:03,105 --> 00:45:03,939
PREVIEW OF THE NEXT EPISODE

603
00:45:04,006 --> 00:45:05,340
…will always be

604
00:45:06,041 --> 00:45:07,676
nothing but garbage.

605
00:45:07,743 --> 00:45:08,977
Subtitle translation by: Lili Morita

